[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1464","stub":{"id":"1464","section":"7 - Carey Creek to Riggins","altname":"","river":"Salmon","difficulty":"IIItoIV","states":["USA-IDA"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"migration-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"37600","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"This access is a popular alternative take-out for the Main Salmon and a put-in for trips on the roadside run down to Riggins. The site has a large parking area and paved ramps providing easy access to the river. It is located at river mile 109.8.","id":"105333","location":{"latitude":"45.45331","longitude":"-115.94568"},"name":"Carey Creek Boat Ramp","distance":"0","photoID":"z49LgQraT5nLI8Wrmt9hh","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"A mid-river rock that creates a hidden hole at flows above 30,000 cfs.","id":"105334","location":{"latitude":"45.427506","longitude":"-116.003739"},"name":"House Rock (aka Block Rock)","distance":"3.47","difficulty":"II","approximate":false,"photoID":"0"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Class II rapid near Van Creek Campground that is a small camping area with toilet facilities. River mile 97.6.","id":"105336","location":{"latitude":"45.426452","longitude":"-116.137638"},"name":"Van Creek Rapids","distance":"11.85","difficulty":"II","approximate":false,"photoID":"0"},{"type":"access","description":"Forest service campground with water, toilets, and paved boat ramp located at Salmon River Road mile 10.5. This is a good access on the paved portion of the Salmon River Road. It is located at river mile 96.9.","id":"105337","location":{"latitude":"45.425161","longitude":"-116.153856"},"name":"Spring Bar","distance":"12.69","photoID":"cveESZWtar0znuX07bqeA","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"Large irregular waves at high water. River mile 94.1.","id":"105338","location":{"latitude":"45.404966","longitude":"-116.193678"},"name":"Ruby Rapids","distance":"15.36","difficulty":"III","approximate":false,"photoID":"0"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Easily recognized by the large yellow bridge over the river just below the rapid. There is a large rock on the top left side of the rapid. At flows above 60,000 cfs this rock creates a large wave called the \"Big Easy\" or \"Haystack.\" At flows below 20,000 cfs, the wave disappears and a large hole forms. At the low flows (around 3000 cfs) of late summer when the rock is fully exposed, the easy line is to the left of the rock. Located at river mile 93.0.","id":"105339","location":{"latitude":"45.399746","longitude":"-116.213339"},"name":"Lake Creek Rapids","distance":"16.45","difficulty":"III","approximate":false,"photoID":"JrJGw2dvhMAeAU0TCAeqg"},{"type":"rapid","description":"This short wave train is a popular location for kayakers at lower flows. River mile 92.1.","id":"105340","location":{"latitude":"45.401513","longitude":"-116.228817"},"name":"Cat's Paw","distance":"17.21","difficulty":"II","approximate":false,"photoID":"0"},{"type":"access","description":"Island Bar Recreation Site is a recreation site administered by the Bureau of Land Management. It is accessible when flows are below 35,000 cfs (at higher flows the site becomes an island). The site is largely undeveloped with dispersed camping and a rough gravel access down to the river at the upstream end of the island. It tends to be a little less busy than the more formal access site at Shorts Bar just downstream. It is a good put-in for those running the town run through Riggins who want to camp the night before.","id":"URtSZbrdUHtcWflKt04SA","location":{"latitude":"45.416177","longitude":"-116.257798"},"name":"Island Bar Recreation Site","distance":"19.1","photoID":"a4jsMn0u1Yge7YRlwjaKJ","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"Shorts Bar is a BLM recreation site with toilets, paved boat ramp, and camp sites (popular with RVs). The large beach is popular for day use. River mile 87.8.","id":"105341","location":{"latitude":"45.414728","longitude":"-116.302145"},"name":"Shorts Bar Recreation Site","distance":"21.69","photoID":"NcGOUwQdILF6PqV03zjKr","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"At flows of approximately 3000-5000 cfs Mill Wave comes in creating a fun play feature just outside Riggins.","id":"Ra78dhjELypvNJrwyteJs","location":{"latitude":"45.41318","longitude":"-116.315531"},"name":"Mill Wave","distance":"22.48","difficulty":"II","approximate":false,"photoID":"I6yRdGIaXsAvZ4dPKgNOC"},{"type":"takeout","description":"Located at Highway 95 mile 195.7 in Riggins City Park recognized by the historic wooden scow, used for one-way trips down the river, that marks the entrance to the park. A ramp provides access to the river. River mile 86.0.","id":"116637","location":{"latitude":"45.425561","longitude":"-116.311617"},"name":"Riggins City Park, Take-Out","distance":"23.4","photoID":"JTmY3vYtP1i3VBHPNY0Qw","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"14815","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7207","description":"","caption":"Lounging at Partridge Creek","poi_name":"Partridge Creek","subject":"Mino the dog","author":"KJK","poi_id":"105333","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14815","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14815"}},{"id":"RZDv5GrKNnrJsEYhWqDfl","ext":"jpg","post_id":"VFYcTjZbQLpsfASVFv8Ul","description":"","caption":"Facilities at Carey Creek Access","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe and Rie Yamazaki","poi_id":"105333","photo_date":"2020-08-30T19:01:20.000Z","updated_at":"2022-11-17T19:01:21.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/RZDv5GrKNnrJsEYhWqDfl","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/RZDv5GrKNnrJsEYhWqDfl"}},{"id":"GAppw0